\begin{abstract}
Codex Journal Volume VII establishes the Dimensional Navigation System,
a suprakernel-governed architecture for traversing Codex layers. The
system integrates glyph-coordinate mapping, dimensional pulse vectors,
inter-layer transition operators, encrypted manifold states, and
stability gradients. This volume formalizes the navigation logic used
